portals.discoverySubtitle = Fragment of Orbis
portals.incomplete.description = <b>The energies within this Fragment have yet to take their final form. All you encounter within - lore, function, and form - awaits its true shape.</b>
portals.hederas_lair.description = Few have experienced the terrors that lurk in Orbis' murkier depths. Fewer still have returned unchanged.\n\
\n\
<msg key="server.portals.incomplete.description"/>
portals.boreal.description = There are frozen forests into which not even an Outlander dares set foot, no matter how the whispers beckon.\n\
\n\
Legends about the region's name pile up: Mountains obscuring the sky, towering trees grazing the clouds, or perhaps ancient creatures born of elemental ice slumbering among the peaks.\n\
\n\
<msg key="server.portals.incomplete.description"/>
portals.henges.description = At times, the line between truth and fiction blurs. Not every Fragment the Ancient Gateway shows you will hold the truths you seek.\n\
\n\
Yet, surely nothing exists without purpose. Perhaps that leads us to a different question: who built these Ancient Gateways, and why?\n\
\n\
<msg key="server.portals.incomplete.description"/>
portals.oasis.description = A Feran values freedom above all else, and nowhere is that freedom embodied more than in the winds of Windrider Valley.\n\
\n\
It was here that they sought refuge in the darkest years of their history, setting up camps where the towering canyon walls might hide them from view.\n\
\n\
<msg key="server.portals.incomplete.description"/>
portals.jungles.description = Deep beneath the desolate wastelands left by an ancient civilization, a primordial haven thrives.\n\
\n\
<msg key="server.portals.incomplete.description"/>
